;; The air-dcs appview Worker. :esm, mirroring cloud-itonami-marketplace-listing,
;; cloud-itonami/app-lo, /app-ongakuka, /app-analytics and gftdcojp/nexus-x402.
;;
;; wrangler.jsonc's main points at dist/worker.js, which is THIS bundle compiled
;; from the source in src/. That is the whole point of the migration recorded in
;; docs/adr/0001: before it, main pointed at svelte/.svelte-kit/cloudflare/_worker.js
;; -- a path with zero matching tracked files, which nothing in the tree builds --
;; while src/app.ts, the file that reads like the application, was referenced by no
;; tracked file at all.
;;
;; :warnings-as-errors is not decoration. shadow treats an undeclared or renamed
;; var as a WARNING, so `shadow-cljs release worker` exits 0 while writing a bundle
;; that throws on its first request. "The build succeeded" is therefore not a check
;; at all -- it cannot fail. Demonstrated in THIS repo before landing this line
;; (docs/operator-quickstart.md S4).
;;
;; The key lives under :compiler-options, NOT :build-options -- shadow reads
;; [:compiler-options :warnings-as-errors] (shadow.build.compiler/should-warning-throw?).
;; Under :build-options it is silently ignored, which is the very failure this
;; option exists to prevent: a fix that cannot fail. scripts/verify-docs-claims.cljs
;; asserts the placement by PARSING this file as EDN, not by grepping it -- a grep
;; would be satisfied by the comment you are reading.
{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}
 :builds
 {:worker
  {:target :esm
   :output-dir "dist"
   :modules {:worker {:exports {default air-dcs.worker/handler}}}
   :compiler-options {:output-feature-set :es2020
                      :infer-externs :auto
                      :warnings-as-errors true}}}}
